------------------------------------------------------
   CSS CLASS SELECTOR — NOTES
---------------------------------------------------------

1. What is a Class Selector?
   - A class selector is used to style one or more HTML elements.
   - It targets elements using a dot (.) followed by the class name.

---------------------------------------------------------
2. Syntax:
     .className {
        property: value;
     }

---------------------------------------------------------
3. Example:
   HTML:
     <p class="highlight">Hello</p>

   CSS:
     .highlight {
        color: red;
        font-weight: bold;
     }
7. Best Practices:
   - Use lowercase class names
   - Use hyphens (btn-primary, card-title)
   - Use meaningful names (not .red-text, better: .warning-text)

---------------------------------------------------------
8. Summary:
   - .classname selects all elements with that class
   - Reusable and flexible
   - Elements can have multiple classes
   - Works well with element selectors

------------------------------------------------------ */
